# Party banter, act 3 (story/banter.gd): one exchange between two or three companions, played now and then on entering an area, once each. Every node opens
# with its act's gate and both speakers, so an exchange that can't be heard comes out empty and is skipped; any file named party_* plays anywhere.
# Drafted by Gemini (docs/plans/gemini_companions/), edited; every edit is listed in the README there. Lines are unvoiced until the voice lane reads them.


~ act3_01_delphine_lucan
if name:delphine_ravelle and name:lucan_houndstooth and flag.act2_done >= 5
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Your spectral hound is staring at my hem again, darling, and Your Foolishness is offering three-to-one odds he chews the velvet before we reach the end of this road.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Barnaby would never savage a lady's wardrobe, Delphine, though I fear my own manners are wearing rather thin at the edges tonight.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Nonsense, you still bow like a headliner before every ambush, even when the cheap seats are throwing teeth at us.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: One keeps up the old courtesies, if you please, because when a gentleman forgets how to bow, the yellow in his eyes takes over the whole posture.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Then I shall keep calling your cue from the wings, until the last curtain comes down on this whole miserable valley.
endif
-> END

~ act3_02_cordelia_silas
if name:cordelia_skein and name:silas_vane and flag.act2_done >= 5
interject name:cordelia_skein: The wind through your ribs has pitched up a full third since the last milepost, Silas, which suggests an acute spike in anticipation or dread.
interject name:silas_vane: Tell's in the twitch, friend, not the ribcage, and a smart player always lets the house think his nerve is fraying before he turns the last card.
interject name:cordelia_skein: You have no pulse for me to chart, yet you have been shuffling those bone slivers at double your baseline ratio for the past hour.
interject name:silas_vane: Look, when you can see the end of the road over the ridge, you either keep your hands moving or you start counting what you owe.
interject name:cordelia_skein: If my hands begin to tremble before the final assay, you have my full permission to mock my calibration.
endif
-> END

~ act3_03_tobin_silas
if name:tobin_hayward and name:silas_vane and flag.act2_done >= 5
interject name:tobin_hayward: Keep that brass censer on your windward flank, Silas, my burlap is bone-dry and I have no wish to go up like a beacon before the finish.
interject name:silas_vane: Relax, friend, I banked the bitter herbs an hour back and I've been hauling this leaky bucket of ditch water three paces behind you just in case.
interject name:tobin_hayward: You carried a bucket of ditch water up a mud trail with your knuckles split and never even tried to charge me a copper for it?
interject name:silas_vane: Don't go getting misty about it, you old sack of hay, I just need someone left standing to tell me my pulse is skipping when we're done.
interject name:tobin_hayward: You haven't got a pulse in those ribs, you daft fraud, though your collar seam is holding together better than most.
endif
-> END

~ act3_04_rook_lucan
if name:rook_coldwake and name:lucan_houndstooth and flag.act2_done >= 5
interject name:rook_coldwake: Your phantom hound is parked square on my greave again, Lucan, which breaks three separate municipal leash statutes even in an unincorporated hollow.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Do forgive him, Rook, he only seeks out cold iron when he scents a particularly foul draught rolling down from the ridge.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Either it is a doom-laden draught or I dropped a crust of kettle corn in my boot cuff before we marched.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Good heavens, he has no eye for dignity tonight, though I confess it eases my mind to walk beside someone whose shield never wavers.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Settle down now, the Watch does not abandon a post just because the neighbours have poor posture.
endif
-> END

~ act3_05_delphine_cordelia
if name:delphine_ravelle and name:cordelia_skein and flag.act2_done >= 5
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Eight sleeves cut on the bias, darling, and not a single pucker at the shoulder seam. I would pay good money to see that pattern.
interject name:cordelia_skein: And your cuff repairs are remarkably neat, Delphine, considering you stitched them mid-stride with a needle that looks suited for sailcloth.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: A girl has to keep her stuffing tucked in when the road gets rough, or the critics start calling the whole act threadbare.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Quite right, darling, if we are to dissect whatever waits at the end of this lane, we ought to arrive with impeccable tailoring.
endif
-> END

~ act3_06_tobin_rook
if name:tobin_hayward and name:rook_coldwake and flag.act2_done >= 5
interject name:tobin_hayward: You have planted that coffin-lid between my boots and a drift of hot cinders again, Rook, and you didn't even break step to do it.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Unattended embers on a public footway are a clear zoning hazard, Tobin, and dry straw catches faster than damp bone.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Most watchmen wouldn't count a bundle of old twine and field mice as worth scorching their brass knocker over.
interject name:rook_coldwake: If you walked out of the Express's crash with us, you are on my shift log, and nobody on my shift log burns while I can lift a slab.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Hold still when we make camp tonight, then, because the leather strap on your shield arm is fraying right through.
endif
-> END

~ act3_07_silas_lucan
if name:silas_vane and name:lucan_houndstooth and flag.act2_done >= 5
interject name:silas_vane: Ten to one the next ugly thing out of the brush lunges for the lantern first, Lucan, I'll keep asking until you crack.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: A gentleman still does not wager on the quarry, Silas, though based on the sloppy spoor in this mud, I cannot award it higher than a four out of ten.
interject name:silas_vane: Four out of ten is generous when my own shadow is hugging my heels tighter than your ghost dog.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: One says "tighter than your hound does", if you please, though I admit the dark ahead has teeth enough to rattle any man's grammar.
interject name:silas_vane: Stick close to my left rib when we hit the door, and we'll see whose manners hold out longer.
endif
-> END

~ act3_08_lucan_rook_tobin
if name:lucan_houndstooth and name:rook_coldwake and name:tobin_hayward and flag.act2_done >= 5
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: The air off the Hollow tastes of rusted iron and wet cellar stone tonight, friends, a prime specimen of bad weather.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Subsoil drainage has given out altogether along this stretch, and my knuckles are taking the damp poorly.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Rub your grave-wax into the knuckles before the chill sets deeper, Rook, and Lucan, stop sniffing the blight like it's vintage cider.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: One must catalogue the bouquet of the night, Tobin, especially when your own turnip lantern and dry straw remain a steady nine out of ten for comfort.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Keep that lantern three paces clear of his cuffs all the same, we have one more docket to clear before we rest.
endif
-> END

~ act3_09_silas_delphine_cordelia
if name:silas_vane and name:delphine_ravelle and name:cordelia_skein and flag.act2_done >= 5
interject name:silas_vane: Look at the crone on that moon tonight, grinning down like she holds every marked card in the shoe and knows our tabs are due.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Let her grin, darling, Your Foolishness has been whispering terrible riddles about her all evening and I intend to spoil her final act.
interject name:cordelia_skein: If both of you intend to spit in the eye of local pathology, do keep your voices steady so my silk notes do not dissolve prematurely.
interject name:silas_vane: House always wins, unless you burn the house, and I couldn't ask for better company to strike the match.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: We are walking out of this valley together, even if Cordelia has to stitch us back up by hand.
endif
-> END
